line	<str>Take:</str>
line	
line	<str>Add a beam to the platform.</str>
line	
line	<str>Put the engine on the engine platform.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you haven't yet, add your five coal to the engine.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the lift and take the plank.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the tunnel, run east, and use your rope on the rock.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the diary from the fire remains.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your plank to cross the rocks, be sure to collect all diary pages by searching the four additional fires through the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Continue running and avoid the steam vents as they will damage you.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read the diary and continue through the crevice, watch the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Armod.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Follow the passage north and enter the crevice at the end of the passage</col>
step	33	-	Quick guide step 33
line	<str>Speak to Advisor Ghrim. (fairy ring code CIP)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Princess Astrid or Prince Brand (depending on who you married), watch the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to King Vargas.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Gardener Gunnhild by the flax patch next to the castle entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Queen Sigrid.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Matilda in/around the southern building inside the castle's walls.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Queen Sigrid.</str>
line	
line	<str>Now is a good time to gear up at the bank at the north part of Etceteria as you won't be coming back here until after the boss fight. Don't forget to take an antipoison to help with the fight. Also take 5 coal or have at least 5 empty spaces. Note: Do not waste time trying to mine coal near Miner Magnus, as you don't actually get any resources. An area to mine coal is provided later on in the quest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to King Vargas.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Advisor Ghrim.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Sailor at the Miscellania docks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to King Vargas with one open inventory slot to receive a scroll proving you are Regent of Miscellania.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the dungeon, down the ladder in the courtyard (along the castle's south wall).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Donal in the pub.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go north, take a pick (on the rock next to the dwarves) if you need coal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the mining prop on the crevice and proceed through the crevice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take an engine and put the 5 coal in it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the following from the crates:</str>
line	
line	<str>Use a beam on a pulley beam to get a long pulley beam; use another regular beam on it to make a longer pulley beam.</str>
line	
line	<str>To the broken scaffold add:</str>
line	
line	<str>Take:</str>
line	
line	<str>Add a beam to the platform.</str>
line	
line	<str>Put the engine on the engine platform.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you haven't yet, add your five coal to the engine.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the lift and take the plank.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the tunnel, run east, and use your rope on the rock.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the diary from the fire remains.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your plank to cross the rocks, be sure to collect all diary pages by searching the four additional fires through the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Continue running and avoid the steam vents as they will damage you.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read the diary and continue through the crevice, watch the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Armod.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the passage north and enter the crevice at the end of the passage</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Kill the <col=800000>Giant Sea Snake</col>. Use protect from ranged prayer and attack at a distance (magic preferred).</col>
